# transient per-run source pulls — never committed (see ../CLAUDE.md)
raw/

# BUILD ARTIFACT, not data. offer/build_data.py regenerates it offline from the
# committed listings.csv in about a second, it is 1.4 MB, and it changes on EVERY
# scrape — committing it would add ~75 MB of churn a year to a public repo for a file
# nothing needs. Same reasoning as raw/: transient and reproducible.
#
# data.js is NOT ignored, deliberately: it is 3x smaller, changes only when the sold
# data does (rarely), and index.html white-screens without it — so a fresh clone should
# just work. The Pages workflow re-bakes it anyway, so a stale commit can't publish
# numbers that disagree with the CSVs behind them.
offer/listings.js
# same reasoning: 3.9 MB, regenerated offline from the committed share/sales.csv in a
# second, and it changes whenever the sold data does. CI rebuilds it before deploying.
offer/sold.js
# same: 143 KB, regenerated offline from committed boundaries + share data.
offer/map.js

# python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# secrets backstop (this repo is PUBLIC)
.env*
*secret*
*webhook*
*.key
*.pem

# private/ — everything personal lives in ONE place, and one rule covers all of it:
# working notes and plans, the buyer-requirements docs (budget, household detail),
# the buyer-brief/ sources plus the script that stitches them, and the Claude Project
# export (the same buyer/budget detail, just split across many files). One directory
# means there is no "which pattern catches this?" question when a new note is written
# — if it is personal, it goes in private/ and it is already ignored.
private/

# Backstop, deliberately kept after the rule above: if a .LOCAL file is ever written
# OUTSIDE private/ by habit, these still catch it before it reaches a commit. This
# repo is PUBLIC — two overlapping rules cost nothing, one missed file costs a lot.
*.LOCAL.md
*.LOCAL.txt
*.LOCAL.py

# The priorities page WRITES priorities.json — your own answers about what you want
# in a house and where you'd bend. Same class as the .LOCAL docs above: personal, and
# this repo is public. The tool (README/serve.py/priorities.html) is committed; your
# answers are not. Guarded before the file exists rather than after.
priorities/priorities.json
